# World 0 — environment template (cognitive core library).
#
# World 0 is a library and has no loader of its own: credentials are read
# from the process environment by the LLM provider classes and by the
# eval harnesses in `scripts/`. Copy this file and source it, or export
# the variables however you prefer:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   set -a && . ./.env && set +a
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. Set only the providers you actually use — the
# whole concept-world works without any of them except the LLM-judged
# paths: text extraction (`World.ingest_text`), similarity judging and
# relation typing (see CLAUDE.md Rule 8).
#
# Launcher and application settings (provider routing, store path, host /
# port, the web + gui extras) moved with `start.sh` to the separate
# **world0-pkm** project in the repository split; they are not read here.

# ── Azure OpenAI — recommended default ───────────────────────────────
# Default extraction model: gpt-5.4-nano, where the model name is the
# Azure *deployment* name (docs/extraction-model-prompt-eval.md).
# Placeholders are quoted so this file stays safe to `source` as shipped:
# unquoted <...> would be read as a shell redirection.
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT="https://<your-resource>.openai.azure.com/"
AZURE_OPENAI_KEY="<your-azure-openai-key>"
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY="<alias accepted too>"

# ── OpenAI (api.openai.com) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by the openai SDK.  Install: pip install -e ".[openai]"
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ── Anthropic (Claude) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by the anthropic SDK.  Install: pip install -e ".[anthropic]"
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CLAUDE_API_KEY="<alias accepted by scripts/eval_extraction_matrix.py>"

# ── Zhipu GLM (OpenAI-compatible; eval harness only) ─────────────────
# Used only by scripts/eval_extraction_matrix.py for cross-model runs.
# GLM_API_KEY=...

# ── Optional outbound proxy (if your network needs one) ──────────────
# Use an HTTP proxy; a SOCKS proxy needs `pip install httpx[socks]`.
# HTTP_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
